WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
Good morning, Hank; it's Tuesday. So one of my favorite YouTubers, CGP Grey- link in the dooblydoo-

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.540
recently did a video debunking ten popular misconceptions.

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:09.840
This inspired me to want to debunk more misconceptions!

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:11.120
For instance, number one:

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.760
The Quran says "all martyrs get 72 virgins in Heaven."

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:15.520
Yeah, the Quran doesn't say that.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:19.740
That tradition comes from a Hadith, which are collections of sayings of the prophet, Muhammad.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:21.740
And that particular Hadith is really poorly sourced.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:29.040
It's like "I heard from a guy, who talked to a guy, and his cousin was all like that the prophet had said like 72 virgins or something!"

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:31.680
Furthermore, Hank, there are some people that argue that the word "virgins"

00:00:31.689 --> 00:00:36.160
is being mistranslated here and that
the actual translation is like "white grapes."

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:39.600
Misconception number two: .999 repeating is less than 1.

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:42.800
In fact, .999 repeating is equal to one, which you know because

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:46.870
.333 repeating is equal to one-third, and one-third plus

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:49.550
one-third plus one-third is 1.

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:53.680
Misconception number three: Ostriches bury their head in the sand to hide from predators.

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:57.040
Incorrect. They bury their
heads in the sand because they have to dig nests,

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:59.360
and they don't have hands with
which to dig.

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:01.760
Misconception number four: sharks don't get cancer,

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.360
so you should eat shark to keep yourself from getting
cancer.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:09.680
In fact, sharks do get cancer, although we don't know how often because everyone is always killing them.

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:14.000
Misconception number five: there is an edge to the universe.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.480
So, Hank, during the last week of our tour, you became obsessed with the fact that

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:20.020
there is no edge to the universe, but
instead of saying it like that,

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:23.360
you just kept saying, "Dude, no edge!"

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:26.800
And you kept accusing me of being inadequately fascinated about the lack

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:31.180
of edge-ness in the universe, when in
fact it was your portrayal of this fact

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:33.960
that was so annoying to me because
you'd just be like eating a sandwich or

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:37.740
something, and you'd turn to me and be like, "Hey, John. There is no edge."

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:41.430
But anyway, yes; apparently there is no edge to the universe. I still don't understand how that

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:43.510
works, but I'm sure that you will explain
it to me.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:46.560
Misconception number six: Albert Einstein failed mathematics.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:52.160
No, he didn't. Albert Eistein was really really good at mathematics. In fact, to quote him,

00:01:52.190 --> 00:01:55.440
"Before I was fifteen, I had mastered differential calculus."

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:59.200
Misconception number seven: Al Gore claimed to have invented the internet.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:02.720
No, he didn't. He claimed to have "taken the initiative in creating the internet,"

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:05.200
which is also an
exaggeration, but just not-not the same

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.920
exaggeration that people accuse him of.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:09.000
Misconception number eight:

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:12.840
Late in the winter of your seventeenth year, you are seventeen.

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:16.040
No, late in the winter of your first year, you are still zero,

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:19.760
late in the winter of your second year, you are one, and late in the winter of your seventeenth year,

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:21.529
you are sixteen.

00:02:21.529 --> 00:02:24.409
Misconception number nine: humans have five senses.

00:02:24.409 --> 00:02:28.169
Wrong. Humans have way more than five senses. The five senses were identified by Aristotle,

00:02:28.169 --> 00:02:35.040
and here's a little rule of thumb: Aristotle, while he is very famous and everything, is almost always wrong.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:38.320
In addition to the five senses we all know, you can also sense relative temperature,

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:42.320
which is called thermoception, you can sense body and limb position,

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:44.660
and you can sense balance, which is called equilibrioception.

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:47.780
You can also sense the need to go deeper, which is called inception.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:51.680
Sorry. I apologize. I apologize to my whole family for that.

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:55.020
Misconception number ten: George Washington had wooden dentures.

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:57.560
No, alas, his dentures were far more disturbing than that.

00:02:57.560 --> 00:03:03.540
They were made of gold, lead, hippopotamus, ivory, dead people teeth, and donkey teeth.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:04.960
Link in the dooblydoo to the original video.

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:08.520
Also, to Michael Aranda's brilliant video of Hank saying "no edge" over and over again.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:11.960
Also, have you seen our new show, Crash course? We're teaching you about stuff! Here's a preview.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:16.720
The test will measure whether you are an informed, engaged, and productive citizen of the world,

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:22.360
and it will take place in schools, and bars, and hospitals, and dormrooms, and in places of worship.

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:25.960
The test will judge your ability to think about things other than celebrity marriages,

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:29.140
whether you'll be easily persuaded by empty political rhetoric,

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:33.340
and whether you'll be able to place your life and your community in a broader context.

00:03:33.349 --> 00:03:37.389
The test will last your entire life, and it will be comprised of the millions of decisions,

00:03:37.389 --> 00:03:44.669
that when taken together make your life yours, and everything - everything - will be on it.

00:03:44.669 --> 00:03:48.359
(Crash Course outro music)

00:03:48.359 --> 00:03:51.666
Hank, I hope you're feeling better! Don't forget to be awesome. I will see you on Friday!

